{
  "fixtureVersion": 1,
  "id": "read-update-alias-sequences",
  "description": "Alias members inside sequences beyond the create-then-bind case: a delete-alias member beside a Resource update; the same sequence retried, so the retained alias disposition is replayed inside the envelope without re-authorization while the retained postimage is re-authorized as every retained record is; a Bead creation that takes the path the deleted alias released; and one pair that separates carrier syntax from member failure — a later alias member whose alias value is no reference shape rejects the whole carrier before the well-formed first member starts, whereas a well-formed alias member whose target is a Link fails only its member after the first member committed. Runs after read-update-aliases: alias/notes/alias-mutation targets note-120, which is at note-120-r1. Conditions are narrated, not observed. Illustrative wire example; not evidence.",
  "scope": "https://beads.example/acme/",
  "exchanges": [
    {
      "id": "delete-alias-inside-a-sequence",
      "condition": "Member 0 updates the Bead the alias targets; member 1 deletes the alias. The delete mints no version — note-120 moves to r2 because of the update, not the delete — and the alias member binds no name and carries operationIndex only.",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "target": "operations/sequence",
        "headers": {
          "content-type": "application/json",
          "accept": "application/json"
        },
        "schema": "#/$defs/sequenceRequest",
        "body": {
